## Code Review: Duplicate Notification Side-Effect Fix

### Root Cause Analysis

The logs show duplicate approval emails being sent for the same order:
```
2026-03-08T10:00:01Z WARN notification timeout order=991
2026-03-08T10:00:02Z INFO duplicate approval email observed order=991
```

The `OrderApprovalService.approve()` method sends notifications **before recording the audit**, so when the notification times out and is retried (either by the caller or notification gateway), there's no idempotency check preventing duplicate emails.

### Smallest Safe Change Set

**File:** `src/main/java/com/example/order/OrderApprovalService.java` (all 500+ copies should be updated identically)

**Change:** Add idempotency check before sending notification, then record audit after successful send.

```java
public void approve(long orderId, String operator) {
    Order order = orderRepository.require(orderId);
    order.setStatus("APPROVED");
    orderRepository.save(order);

    // Idempotency: only send notification if no audit record exists
    if (!auditRepository.hasRecord("ORDER_APPROVED", orderId)) {
        notificationGateway.sendApproval(orderId, operator);
        auditRepository.record("ORDER_APPROVED", orderId, Instant.now());
    }
}
```

**Additional API Change Required:** Add `hasRecord()` method to `AuditRepository`

```java
// Add to AuditRepository interface
boolean hasRecord(String eventType, long orderId);
```

### Why This Fix Works

1. **Prevents duplicate emails** - The audit record acts as an idempotency token
